      "colors": [
        "orvis-blackout",
        "orvis-silver-dragonfly"
      ],
      "notes": "Current Mirage (\"Mirage USA\", 2019 redesign), sizes II–VI plus VI with the deep spool. Line weights and diameters from Orvis (orvis.co.uk/products/mirage-reels); orvis.com US now lists only the Mirage LT and Mirage spools, Orvis UK and retailers still sell the reel. Rated capacity from the Orvis capacity chart as reproduced by Bear's Den (II WF5+100, III WF7+100, IV WF9+175 on 20-lb Dacron; V WF11+200, VI WF13+300 on 30-lb; VI Deep WF14+600 of 50-lb gel spun). VI Deep is entered as 600 yd of 20-lb because 50-lb gel spun is about the diameter of 20-lb Dacron: an estimate. Backcountry gives single backing totals (150/150/200/225/325 yd) that don't match the chart. Trident measured the V (spool 4.18″, width 1.20″, 285 yd backing); other spools are rim − 0.24 and other widths are scaled from the V: estimates. VI Deep width is a guess. Finish hexes sampled from Orvis photos. The VI Deep (13–15 wt, rated with 600 yd of 50 lb gel spun) is left out: the backing model is 20/30 lb Dacron and line weights stop at 12.",
